WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.020
The final page brings the frozen
assessment and historical replay together

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.050
at loopback port eight five zero four.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.930
Seven model rows,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.760
counted monthly summaries and three
predeclared examples make the final

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.410
finding inspectable.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.620
The group row retains the original
selection badge even though the forest has

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.910
lower final error.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.400
Original model and bundle
hashes remain unchanged,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.830
with protocol identity and
attribution available in the details.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.310
Loading the page does not
refit or select another model.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.760
The application connects displayed numbers
to the saved function and assessment

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.570
procedure, while keeping
their limitations visible.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.580
Final Application loads the existing
saved predictor and separate replay

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.330
observations,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.710
then checks the completed assessment.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.470
The protocol hash, selected model
and bundle context must agree,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.010
and retained assessment artifact
hashes must still match.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.220
A changed evidence file fails before
serving rather than producing a plausible

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.250
table from mismatched assets.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.320
The server binds locally
and uses packaged web files,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.450
with no model training on startup.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.320
An isolated installed wheel works with
copied assets while an audit hook denies

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.310
all source project file opens.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.670
That verifies portable packaged behavior
without claiming an external deployment.

00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:35.757
The final batch can evaluate July through
December because its feature rows were

00:01:35.757 --> 00:01:36.747
already frozen,

00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:38.967
including source calendar flags.

00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:44.697
The interactive predictor has a separately
saved January through June recorded

00:01:44.697 --> 00:01:46.027
holiday authority.

00:01:46.697 --> 00:01:48.347
We retain that request boundary.

00:01:48.897 --> 00:01:51.307
A July request is therefore rejected

00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:54.807
even though July appears
in the evaluation table.

00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:59.577
This is an explicitly named scope
distinction rather than an accidental

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.027
hidden limitation.

00:02:01.637 --> 00:02:06.217
Possessing later batch features does not
create unrestricted knowledge of future

00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:09.247
holidays or a production
forecasting service.

00:02:09.677 --> 00:02:14.337
Extending serving would need its own
trusted calendar contract and evidence,

00:02:14.337 --> 00:02:17.167
rather than silently
changing this artifact.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:22.037
On the real January ninth request,

00:02:22.387 --> 00:02:25.827
the predictor returns three hundred
and forty nine point five zero four,

00:02:25.827 --> 00:02:28.977
with no observed outcome in its response.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:33.347
Clicking Show recorded outcome separately
retrieves four hundred and twenty and

00:02:33.347 --> 00:02:37.637
displays residual negative
seventy point five zero.

00:02:38.847 --> 00:02:42.487
A valid unrecorded January second
hour still receives an estimate,

00:02:42.487 --> 00:02:46.257
while actual count and
residual remain unavailable.

00:02:46.947 --> 00:02:49.437
Changing the input clears old output,

00:02:49.647 --> 00:02:53.997
and unsupported dates cannot leave
a stale successful forecast visible.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:59.047
Browser checks exercise those
paths at desktop and mobile widths,

00:02:59.047 --> 00:03:02.637
keeping prediction availability
separate from observation coverage.

00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:10.653
The earlier linear Adam demonstration
preserves parameters, scaler, moments,

00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:13.193
update index, batch order,

00:03:13.583 --> 00:03:17.413
cursor, random state,
schedule and monitoring context.

00:03:18.023 --> 00:03:23.653
It resumes the same numerical continuation
after explicit damaged save fallback.

00:03:23.863 --> 00:03:25.713
That is a reproduction result.

00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:30.113
The final table measures
forecasting error on later hours,

00:03:30.323 --> 00:03:34.073
while browser and package checks
measure usable local behavior.

00:03:34.623 --> 00:03:38.053
Each matters,
but one cannot substitute for the others.

00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:43.063
Exact recovery can preserve a poorly
fitting run or an inaccurate forecast

00:03:43.063 --> 00:03:43.913
perfectly.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:47.813
This final assessment adds
no new training result,

00:03:47.883 --> 00:03:51.213
hosted recovery proof or
calibrated predictive uncertainty.

00:03:53.688 --> 00:03:57.118
The local route now includes
provenance and splits,

00:03:57.588 --> 00:03:59.818
model calculations and comparisons,

00:04:00.488 --> 00:04:02.418
saved inference, recovery,

00:04:03.068 --> 00:04:03.498
replay

00:04:04.108 --> 00:04:05.918
and a frozen final assessment.

00:04:07.128 --> 00:04:11.088
One hundred and twenty two checks and
independent audits pass while substantial

00:04:11.088 --> 00:04:12.458
deficits remain.

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:16.298
The complete written records
preceded these short companions.

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:20.838
They consolidate prior study
rather than prove learner mastery.

00:04:21.688 --> 00:04:24.378
No hosted recovery, remote publication

00:04:24.768 --> 00:04:27.078
or next project implementation occurred.

00:04:27.888 --> 00:04:29.878
The next conversation is concrete:

00:04:30.608 --> 00:04:32.298
if we choose the forest now,

00:04:32.568 --> 00:04:36.058
what can we honestly claim and
what new evidence would we need?

00:04:36.728 --> 00:04:41.148
Answering connects the final result to the
development procedure without requiring

00:04:41.148 --> 00:04:42.298
routine typing.

